docs/concepts/components.md:37:`Subscribes`/`Publishes` are the asynchronous (message) edges; `From`/`To` are the edges out through ports that the flow starts or ends at; `LooksUp` is a port consulted mid-flow, request/response, for enrichment — the subscription, not the port, drives the component; `Calls` records Dapr service app IDs the component invokes. A component may publish several distinct messages — several may share one channel; publishing the same message twice throws `InvalidOperationException` at the declaration. See [Messages](messages.md), [Ports](ports.md), and the [Model and DSL Reference](model.md).
docs/concepts/ports.md:36:Direction is not part of a port's identity — it follows from usage: `From(port)` reads (the port drives the flow), `To(port)` writes, `LooksUp(port)` consults it mid-flow for enrichment (`Lookup`; at the Dapr level an output-binding invocation such as `get`, never a trigger). Because the name is the identity, two declarations with the same name are the same port by construction; there is nothing left to conflict.
